import pickle,itertools
S=pickle.load(open('certs2.pkl','rb'))
base={}
for c in itertools.combinations(range(14),7):
 a=sum(1<<i for i in c);b=1
 for i in range(14):
  if not (a>>i&1):b|=b<<(1<<i)
 base[a]=b
low=[0,128,192,224,240,248,252,254,256,272,288,296,304,308,312,314,316,318,320,324,328,332]
# Some low certificates were not hit in original random search, recover from four-flat data.
F=pickle.load(open('four.pkl','rb'))
for w in low:
 if w in S:continue
 ov,cs,ds=F[w]
 caps=[ov,7-ov,7-ov,ov];pat=[3,1,2,0];ns=[];ps=[]
 for n,c,p in zip(caps,cs,pat):ns.extend([c,n-c]);ps.extend([p|4,p])
 ms=[0]*4;var=0
 for n,d,p in zip(ns,ds,ps):
  for pp,nn in [(p|8,d),(p,n-d)]:
   for _ in range(nn):
    for j in range(4):
     if pp>>j&1:ms[j]|=1<<var
    var+=1
 S[w]=[(a,a) for a in ms]
target=low+list(range(336,8193,2))
for w in target:
 f=0
 for a,x in S[w]:
  assert a.bit_count()==7 and (x&a)==x
  f^=base[a]<<x
 assert f.bit_count()==w,(w,f.bit_count())
print('Independently verified',len(target),'explicit codeword witnesses; all have degree at most 7 in 14 variables.')
pickle.dump({w:S[w] for w in target},open('verified.pkl','wb'))

